//? Title: Temporal FCN:raw signals,explicit Adam and calibrated BN
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Three temporal8/5/3 convolution blocks classify genuine GunPoint hand motions. Tensor-only preprocessing,an explicit SGD centroid reference,all Adam updates and paired learned/BN/normalization restoration expose the distinction between minibatch training and calibrated frozen inference.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.9_1d_convolutions/time_series_cnn.cpp`.

> The method

Retain the original official test records,compute fitting-only population normalization,and train a complete temporal FCN with hard-label CE. Calibrate BN sequentially on fitting observations after each epoch;validation selects the paired learned/state checkpoint. Compare raw1NN and explicitly SGD-fitted centroid fields using tensor metrics and original source signal plots.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/time_series_cnn_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/time_series_cnn_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/time_series_cnn_concept.tikz > build/time_series_cnn_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/time_series_cnn_concept.svg build/time_series_cnn_concept.dvi > build/time_series_cnn_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
