> Even-kernel SAME padding has a visible phase

The first kernel has width8. SAME,stride1,pads3 values on the left and4 on
the right,then performs cross-correlation. Kernels5 and3 pad symmetrically.
All three blocks preserve the150-sample time axis. The declared impulse
fixture displays the exact width8 response and its input adjoint;these are
not trained features or real observations.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/time_series_cnn_padding.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  const auto impulse =
      n::one_hot(n::full({1}, 3., n::DType::Int64), 7).reshape({1, 7, 1}).requires_grad_();
  const auto kernel = n::arange(1, 9).reshape({8, 1, 1});
  const auto y = n::conv1d(impulse, kernel);
  const auto g = n::grad(n::sum(y), {impulse})[0];
  std::print("Width8 SAME:3left/4right pads,impulse response {},input adjoint {}.\n",
             y.reshape({7}), g.reshape({7}));
  const auto positions = n::arange(0, 7).to_vector<double>();
  auto a = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), b = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  a.bars(positions, y.reshape({7}).to_vector<double>(), "response", {37, 99, 235})
      .title("Declared even8 impulse response")
      .x_label("preserved temporal position")
      .y_label("cross-correlation value");
  b.bars(positions, g.reshape({7}).to_vector<double>(), "input adjoint", {220, 38, 38})
      .title("Exact sum-output input derivative")
      .x_label("original temporal position")
      .y_label("sum of supported kernel weights");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 500).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/time_series_cnn_padding.svg");
}
```
