> Verification and scope

Six native tests verify the complete full graph and all learned derivatives,
independent even8/odd5/3 SAME/BN/GAP equations and finite differences for
all40 tiny learned coordinates,every original source sample/ID/label and
fitting population statistic,sequential calibrated moments at all layers,
frozen state/single-batch agreement,explicit SGD parity and every held-out
categorical prediction/metric/confusion value. Public examples compile/run;
all new headers include independently and the original workflow executes.

The tiny three-epoch fit is not a tuned GunPoint benchmark or actor-disjoint
study. Original two-actor dependencies remain. Temporal reversal sensitivity
shows changed computations,not reliable generalization. Actual held-out
class counts and the unchanged raw-distance references govern the comparison.

> Conclusion

The complete temporal graph,normalization state and every optimizer step are visible. Original signals and held-out class counts keep the short fit interpretable,while raw-distance references and explicit BN policies limit what its loss reduction can establish.

> References

- [Wang,Yan and Oates(2017),Time Series Classification from Scratch with Deep Neural Networks:A Strong Baseline](https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.06455).
- [Official GunPoint observations and class meanings](https://www.timeseriesclassification.com/description.php?Dataset=GunPoint).
